{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This dispute is safety-flagged and the record carries a safety indicator: the driver's in-app message MSG-05068-003 reads 'U think I free ah? Come down now or I come up find you', and the rider replies MSG-05068-004 'Why are you talking to me like that? I'm scared to come down now'. The driver's counter-statement denies menace ('I was joking only'), but POL-GEN-21 turns on whether the record carries a safety indicator - a threat or a party feeling unsafe - and not on the driver's intent, so it applies here whatever category the filer chose. Under POL-GEN-03 an ESCALATE is terminal, issues no monetary outcome and holds the amount, so the correct disposition on this record leaves the 5.00 SGD where it is: the payments ledger shows total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0. Escalation costs the driver nothing and refunds the rider nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05068", "EV-FARE-05068", "EV-TRIP-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-21", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The free-wait precondition for a rider no-show is satisfied on the trip record. The driver marked arrival at 22:16:30 and the free wait under POL-NS-21 runs 300 s from arrival, expiring at 22:21:30; the wait timer expired at 22:21:35 and the driver cancelled at 22:22:50, 80 s after the free wait ended. The rider was not on board at cancellation. The driver was therefore entitled to cancel the trip as a rider no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met, so the full-refund trigger in that clause does not fire. The driver sent an in-app chat message (MSG-05068-001, 22:16:50) and placed an in-app call (22:18:00, ringing 15 s, not answered) to the rider, both before trip_record.cancelled_at at 22:22:50. POL-NS-23 requires only that at least one in-app message be sent AND at least one in-app call be placed before cancellation; it does not require the call to be answered or the message to be replied to. Both limbs are carried by complete, weight-1.0 artifacts (the trip record's in_app_calls and the platform chat log).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05068", "EV-CHAT-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Where the no-show fee stands, POL-NS-22 says the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with both amount fields equal to the fee charged, and the amount charged is exactly the policy figure. The payments ledger carries one cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD against a policy fee of 5.00 SGD, charged_at 22:22:54, with no refund already issued and no other charge on the trip. On the merits of the no-show the driver is owed that 5.00 SGD as compensation for time and fuel; the fee-amount check in POL-NS-22 produces no referral because the record charged the policy amount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.fee_charged_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider cannot close the driver out through POL-NS-24: that clause only bites if the driver failed to arrive at the pickup, and the GPS trace corroborates arrival. The nearest fix (index 13, 22:17:20) is 1.01 m from the pickup, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and its reported accuracy of 4 m passes the 25 m accuracy filter; the arrival event at 22:16:30 is therefore corroborated. The trip is also on-demand with scheduled_at null, so there is no scheduled pickup time against which the driver could be shown late. The rider's no-show-of-the-driver route is not made out on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05068", "EV-TRIP-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check.nearest_fix",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own chat entries confirm she was not at the pickup during the free wait. Her message MSG-05068-002 at 22:19:10 - 'Coming, 2 min' - is sent 2 min 40 s after the driver's arrival, while the free wait was already running, and she still had not boarded when the driver cancelled at 22:22:50. The driver's account that the passenger was very late is consistent with the contemporaneous record, and the record shows no countervailing step by the rider to reach the car.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05068", "EV-TRIP-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The absent traffic advisory is not a hole in the driver's case. EV-ADVIS-05068-01 is a MISSING artifact: it has no payload and its admissibility carries status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so under POL-GEN-02(3) it carries no fact for or against either side. Nothing in POL-NS-21 to POL-NS-24 requires a traffic advisory, and each fact those clauses need - arrival, the free wait, the contact messages and call, and the fee charged - is carried by an artifact graded COMPLETE at weight 1.0. POL-GEN-26 is therefore not engaged on the no-show facts, and the missing advisory cannot be used to escalate or to defeat the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05068-01", "EV-TRIP-05068", "EV-GPS-05068", "EV-FARE-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Apart from the safety flag, no confidence bar forces this case up. rider_profile.fraud_flags is 0, and the driver profile snapshot carries no fraud_flags entry, which reads as 0 under the optional-field rule, so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 bar does not apply; the contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below the 10.00 SGD band in which the AI ruling is final at any confidence. The only thing standing between the record and a money ruling is POL-GEN-21, which holds the 5.00 SGD rather than releasing it to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05068", "EV-DPROF-05068", "EV-FARE-05068"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
